/-!
# Integer cocycles from actual factor logarithms

The logarithmic defect of a genuine holomorphic factor defines a normalized
integral group two-cocycle.  Explicit canonical logarithms, product factors,
and gauges extracted from actual analytic bundle isomorphisms are compared
with the chosen logarithms by concrete integer branch corrections.

The convention here is the positive factor-log defect.  Its branch change
is the negative standard group coboundary; no identification with a first
Chern class or a choice of topological orientation is made in this module.
-/
